Atikāya sees brothers uncles slain rushes in sunlike chariot --- Atikāya roars name scatters monkeys like Viṣṇu strides --- Monkeys seek refuge as Rāma asks Vibhīṣaṇa who is giant --- Vibhīṣaṇa names son of Dhānyamālinī blessed by Brahmā with armor chariot --- Atikāya shatters trees rocks wounds foremost monkeys --- Atikāya spares nonfighters scorns boy Lakṣmaṇa demands single combat --- Lakṣmaṇa rises exchanges shafts mighty weapons --- Atikāya meets fire with sun reed with Indra south with wind darts --- Lakṣmaṇa shafts shatter on charmed armor --- Vāyu tells Lakṣmaṇa armor yields only to Brahmā weapon --- Lakṣmaṇa looses Brahmā shaft severs crowned head like Himālaya peak